{"skill":{"slug":"skill-creator-2","displayName":"Skill Creator"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769830982484,"changelog":"Initial release of Skill Creator: a comprehensive guide for building effective skills to extend Claude's capabilities.\n\n- Explains the structure and purpose of skills: modular packages with workflows, integrations, and expertise.\n- Outlines core principles including conciseness, proper use of degrees of freedom, and efficient use of the context window.\n- Details required file organization with guidance on when to use SKILL.md, scripts, references, and assets.\n- Emphasizes best practices for maintaining lean, easily discoverable, and usable skills.\n- Describes the progressive disclosure system for loading skill metadata and resources efficiently.\n- Specifies what not to include, reducing clutter and ensuring skills are agent-focused.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":17837,"sha256":"b2e3d83f60425c2d0b9d4162efb8f9aa322b45843497340f2289f42be422801c","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1670,"sha256":"1a2c51cc9003e6203a0f5d8ec8f130db2901d07a69250d204ab646fe254887a5","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789024010354,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3e21071f68dc7ea2b094116cf6bb3ab0f230e0747a57c4ef96a3a1200984cdd2","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3e21071f68dc7ea2b094116cf6bb3ab0f230e0747a57c4ef96a3a1200984cdd2","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: skill-creator-2\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle is classified as benign. The `SKILL.md` file provides instructions for an AI agent to create and manage other skills, including explicit commands to execute local Python scripts (`scripts/init_skill.py` and `scripts/package_skill.py`). While script execution is a high-risk capability, in this context, it is directly aligned with the stated purpose of a 'skill-creator' skill and involves local, bundled scripts rather than remote execution or arbitrary shell access. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, persistence mechanisms, or malicious prompt injection attempts to subvert the agent's core directives.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160359158},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":40,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789024010354},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a markdown-only guide for creating or updating skills, and its file-editing instructions fit that purpose.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The expected local file changes are limited to user-directed skill projects and bundled resources; there is no network retrieval, credential handling, broad indexing, or account mutation.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The package contains only SKILL.md and no install hook, dependencies, or executable payloads; it references helper scripts that are not present in the artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The trigger description is broad but still tied to user requests to create or update a skill; I found no hidden role changes, safety bypasses, or unrelated instructions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact does not install background services, scheduled jobs, memory entries, profile changes, or other persistence mechanisms.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact explains how to design, write, test, and package skills; creating or editing SKILL.md and related resources is coherent with that stated purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Use this when you want agent help building skills. Because it guides the agent to create, edit, delete, test, and package files in a skill project, review the target directory and any generated or tested scripts before relying on the result.","findings":"[RA1] expected: The cited workflow step to write SKILL.md refers to authoring a target skill, not modifying this installed skill at runtime.\n[RA1] expected: The Update SKILL.md section is ordinary skill-authoring guidance; deleting generated example files is scoped to the target skill project.\n[SQP-1] expected: The description could be narrower, but it is bounded to creating or updating skills and does not create a material security concern by itself.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789024010354}}}}}